cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Monolith, please cite it as below."
title: "Monolith: A Spatial Analysis Dashboard for Geostatistical Modeling and Mapping"
abstract: >-
  Monolith is an open-source R/Shiny application for reproducible spatial
  statistical analysis, geostatistical interpolation, and mapping of
  point-referenced environmental data. It provides deterministic and
  geostatistical prediction engines (inverse distance weighting, thin plate
  splines, and ordinary, co-, regression, and random-forest kriging) with
  automated and manual variogram fitting and selectable cross-validation
  strategies (leave-one-out, k-fold, and spatial block), reporting RMSE, MAE,
  R-squared, NSE, CCC, RPD, RPIQ, and Moran's I. Continuous predictions can be
  classified into user-defined zones with per-class area statistics, while
  surface-delta and point-error maps expose the spatial structure of prediction
  error. A separate Classification Suite performs predictive multiclass
  classification of categorical field states from co-sampled covariates
  (multinomial, random-forest, and XGBoost learners) with spatially-aware
  cross-validation and entropy-based uncertainty mapping. Complementary
  descriptive, correlation, PCA, and Random-Forest governing-factor (ALE/PDP)
  modules, together with an export registry, support publication-ready
  output. Monolith targets soil science, agronomy, and related environmental
  disciplines.
